# Claude Code local artifacts (skill cache, isolated worktrees, superpowers shim)
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.superpowers/
# `memory: project` on the ship-* seats writes here. It must be ignored: the
# shipper refuses to ship a tree where `git status --porcelain` is non-empty,
# so an unignored memory dir makes every run block its own Phase 5. Committing
# it instead would put agent notes in the diff of unrelated PRs and conflict
# across concurrent worktrees. Per-developer, like graphify-out/.
.claude/agent-memory/
# Hand-copied ports of the pipeline to other harnesses. Two of these (.agents/,
# .codex/) appeared on 2026-09-08 as untracked snapshots of a pre-#858
# `/ship-spec`, still carrying a `--confirm-promote` flag, a `ship-gate-runner`
# seat and a `phase=halted first` rule that the real skill had already retired.
# A copy cannot be kept honest by discipline. `.claude/` is the single source;
# if another harness is ever needed, GENERATE it and gate the drift in CI.
.agents/
.codex/
graphify-out/*
# `graphify hook install` output — per developer, never committed: with
# core.hooksPath=.githooks it warns on every commit for anyone without graphify.
.githooks/post-commit
.githooks/post-checkout

# Orphan root lockfile (no root pyproject); the real lock is backend/uv.lock
/uv.lock
